SOURCES CONSULTED

  NWFA Installation Guidelines (PDF)
    https://www.floorreports.com/images/technotes_files/54.pdf
  Somerset Hardwood Flooring — solid installation guidelines (states the
  4% strip / 2% plank split and the 60–80 °F / 30–50% RH window explicitly)
    https://www.somersetfloors.com/solid-installation
  Wood Floor Business — "Moisture Testing 101: How To Do It Right On Every Job"
    https://www.woodfloorbusiness.com/installation/moisture/article/15124423/moisture-testing-101-how-to-do-it-right-on-every-job
  Sensora — ASTM limits for concrete under wood flooring (75% RH, 3 lb)
    https://sensorahome.com/blogs/moisture-meter/moisture-content-concrete-for-wood-flooring
  Wagner Meters — ASTM F2170 sensor count per 1,000 sq ft
    https://www.wagnermeters.com/concrete-moisture-test/concrete-info/astm-guideline-rh-sensor/

WHAT I COULD NOT VERIFY

I did not purchase the ASTM F2170 or F1869 standards themselves; the numeric
limits and the test-location rule are taken from the secondary sources above,
which agree with each other. Before this tool is promoted to contractors, the
two ASTM documents should be read directly and the NWFA guidelines confirmed
against the current edition rather than the 2008-era PDF that is freely
mirrored. The thresholds live in one place, lib/moisture.ts, precisely so that
correcting them is a one-line change.

NOTE ON ORDER

Applies on top of FLOORFORGE_43.

